# Plugin: my-plugin
# Description: One-line summary of what this plugin adds to the shell
# Author: Abdullah Masood
# Version: 1.0.0
# Dependencies: None
# Requires: None
# Startup Cost: ~0ms

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW THIS FILE WORKS
#
# Everything ABOVE the first blank line is the metadata header: a contiguous
# block of "# Key: Value" comment lines, in the order shown. The first blank
# line ends the header; everything BELOW it is the plugin body — plain
# PowerShell that runs when the profile loads.
#
# Field guide:
#   Plugin        Unique name. MUST match the folder + file name:
#                 plugins/<name>/<name>.config  (e.g. plugins/my-plugin/my-plugin.config)
#   Description   One short line shown in `listconfigs.ps1`.
#   Author        Your name.
#   Version       Semver. Recorded in the profile marker; bump it on changes.
#   Dependencies  OTHER PLUGINS this one needs, comma-separated (e.g. git-aliases),
#                 or None. addconfig.ps1 offers to install them first.
#   Requires      EXTERNAL TOOLS as "command|winget-id", comma-separated
#                 (e.g. zoxide|ajeetdsouza.zoxide), or None. addconfig.ps1
#                 offers to `winget install` any that are missing.
#   Startup Cost  Rough load-time budget (e.g. ~0ms). Keep it near zero.
#
# Tips:
#   * Prefer defining functions/aliases (cheap) over running commands at load.
#   * If a required tool might be absent, guard your code so the snippet is a
#     harmless no-op:  if (Get-Command foo -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { ... }
#   * Guard interactive-only work (PSReadLine key handlers, prompts) so
#     non-interactive `pwsh -Command` / `-File` runs stay fast.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Example body — replace with your own. Defining a function costs almost
# nothing at startup because nothing actually runs until you call it.
function Show-MyPlugin {
    Write-Host 'my-plugin loaded'
}

